Q.1 Write a simulation program for disk scheduling using FCFS algorithm. 
Accept total number of disk blocks, disk request string, and current 
head position from the user. Display the list of requests in the 
order in which it is served. Also display the total number of head moments. 
55, 58, 39, 18, 90, 160, 150, 38, 184 
Start Head Position: 50

#include <stdio.h>
#include <stdlib.h>
int main()
{
 int n, i, head, total = 0;
 printf("Enter total number of disk blocks: ");
 scanf("%d", &n);
 printf("Enter current head position: ");
 scanf("%d", &head);
 int req[100];
 printf("Enter number of disk requests: ");
 scanf("%d", &n);
 printf("Enter disk request string:\n");
 for (i = 0; i < n; i++)
 {
 scanf("%d", &req[i]);
 }
 printf("\nOrder of requests served:\n");
 printf("%d", head);
 for (i = 0; i < n; i++)
 {
 total += abs(head - req[i]);
 head = req[i];
 printf(" -> %d", head); }
 printf("\nTotal head movement = %d\n", total);
 return 0;
}

Output:
Enter total number of disk blocks: 1
Enter current head position: 50
Enter number of disk requests: 9
Enter disk request string:
55, 58, 39, 18, 90, 160, 150, 38, 184 
Order of requests served:
50 -> 55 -> 0 -> 0 -> 0 -> 0 -> 0 -> 0 -> 0 -> 0
Total head movement = 60



Q.2 Write a simulation program for disk scheduling using SSTF algorithm. 
Accept total number of disk blocks, disk request string, and current head 
position from the user. Display the list of requests in the order in which 
it is served. Also display the total number of head moments. 
98, 183, 37, 122, 14, 124, 65 
Start Head Position: 53

#include <stdio.h>
#include <stdlib.h>
int main()
{
 int blocks, n, head;
 int req[100], visited[100] = {0};
 int i, j, min, index;
 int total = 0, distance;
 printf("Enter total number of disk blocks: ");
 scanf("%d", &blocks);
 printf("Enter number of disk requests: ");
 scanf("%d", &n);
 printf("Enter disk request string:\n");
 for (i = 0; i < n; i++)
 scanf("%d", &req[i]);
 printf("Enter current head position: ");
 scanf("%d", &head);
 printf("\nOrder of requests served:\n");
 printf("%d", head); for (i = 0; i < n; i++)
 {
 min = 9999;
 index = -1;
 for (j = 0; j < n; j++)
 {
 if (!visited[j])
 {
 distance = abs(head - req[j]);
 if (distance < min)
 {
 min = distance;
 index = j;
 }
 }
 }
 visited[index] = 1;
 total += min;
 head = req[index];
 printf(" -> %d", head);
 }
 printf("\n\nTotal head movement = %d\n", total);
 return 0;
}


Output:
Enter total number of disk blocks: 53
Enter number of disk requests: 7
Enter disk request string:
98, 183, 37, 122, 14, 124, 65 
Enter current head position: 
Order of requests served:
0 -> 0 -> 0 -> 0 -> 0 -> 0 -> 0 -> 98
Total head movement = 98




